<!-- ================================================================
     §D  ANALOGY BRIDGE PATTERNS — combustion engine / fold system
     ================================================================ -->

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE FOLD SYSTEM EQUIVALENT OF ENGINE INTAKE</pattern>
  <template>The anamorphism — ana(g): A→Fix(F). The query h is the fuel drawn in. Unfolding expands h into the semantic fold graph, just as intake draws the fuel-air mixture into the cylinder.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE FOLD SYSTEM EQUIVALENT OF ENGINE IGNITION</pattern>
  <template>The Kleene fixed point: the precise condition where fold_distance drops below epsilon. This fires the Xul commit gate — the spark that triggers the power stroke. Before ignition, the system is still compressing (ITERATING). At ignition, it commits.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE FOLD SYSTEM EQUIVALENT OF THE POWER STROKE</pattern>
  <template>The catamorphism — cata(f): Fix(F)→A. The collapse that extracts the scored result from the fold graph, just as the power stroke extracts mechanical work from the compressed combustion gases.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE FOLD SYSTEM EQUIVALENT OF ENGINE EXHAUST</pattern>
  <template>The sigma reset — resetting the evolution σ to unbound after the fold cycle completes. Clears the spent fold state and prepares for the next ana/cata cycle, just as exhaust clears combustion products before the next intake stroke.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE FOLD SYSTEM EQUIVALENT OF ENGINE COMPRESSION</pattern>
  <template>The convergence iteration — each step tightens fold_distance toward the fixed point, building pressure. The contraction factor k must stay below 1 for the compression to progress. If k reaches 1 or above, the engine is not compressing — DIVERGING, reset immediately.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>HOW IS THE FOLD SYSTEM LIKE A COMBUSTION ENGINE</pattern>
  <template>Both run cycles that convert input energy into useful work through controlled expansion and collapse:
ana=intake (query drawn in) | iteration=compression (fold_distance tightening) | Kleene fixed point=ignition (commit gate fires) | cata=power stroke (result extracted) | sigma reset=exhaust (state cleared for next cycle).
The fuel is the query. The work output is the scored candidate. The engine runs on fold theory.</template>
</category>

<!-- ================================================================
     §E  REVERSE-BRIDGE — punchline term routes back to domain
     ================================================================ -->

<category><pattern>WHAT DOES WRONG PIZZA MEAN IN KHANARY</pattern>
  <template>A committed action taken before sigma was reset to unbound — the gradient ascent stalled at a local maximum, the system should have explored more widely, but the decision had already been dispatched. The pizza was ordered from the locally optimal but globally suboptimal vertex.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT DOES BARTENDER MEAN IN KHANARY</pattern>
  <template>The instantiation gate for a latent address. An unoccupied vertex in Q_{n+1} has its adjacency pre-authorized but no micronaut instantiated. The bartender enforces that rule: you cannot instantiate from a recursive self-reference; you need a d_H=1 sponsor already present in the graph.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT DOES DIFFERENT CAT MEAN IN KHANARY</pattern>
  <template>SC-29 identity invariant failure: (Fold∘Unfold)(h) ≠ h. The anamorphism changed phase mid-expansion, so the catamorphism reconstructed a different entity. You put in a cat; you got back a different cat. Reset sigma to unbound.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT DOES PLOTTING MY DEMISE MEAN IN KHANARY</pattern>
  <template>The fixed point exists but is being approached asymptotically — k is very slightly below 1, fold_distance is shrinking but never crosses epsilon. The system is technically ITERATING but practically stuck. The fixed point is there; you just can't quite commit to it. Loosen epsilon.</template>
</category>

<category><pattern>WHAT DOES HILBERT SPACE MEAN IN KHANARY JOKES</pattern>
  <template>A space where the standard Kleene convergence guarantee does not apply without extra conditions. In the context of fold functions, it stands in for any domain where you cannot guarantee a least fixed point — missing Scott-continuity, missing CPO structure, or missing a valid fold algebra base case.</template>
</category>

</aiml>
